                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Purpose: UTCI at sensors on a circular patch for single hours, with machine-learning wind.
Fidelity: Screening - machine-learning wind (Yel 2.0); buildings only, no trees.
Method: Wind Predictor at 7 m/s for 8 directions, VAF per Atlanta hour; MRT View Factors (192 sky patches, Fast) and MRT Solve feed UTCI (Simulation).
Result: UTCI per sensor; Deconstruct UTCI reduces it to statistics.
Needs: Nothing to install; ML Model downloads Yel 2.0 on first use. Runtime: minutes.
Edit: Context Brep, sensor patch, weather file; add trees to model their shade.</item>
                  </items>
